sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-simulans-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-simulans-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-simulans-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila simulans 1.92 µm Turing carrier on the posterior-lobe arc (pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 88.8/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the same dispersion law (λ_c = 1.92 µm at γ = 1.428) and reports the odd-radius holdout Pearson r = 0.9895, RMSE 4.07 against a null RMSE 28.16, and KS 0.096. Plate CV similarity of the 12-frame GIF is 89.5; the Wikimedia whole-fly control is 85.6, so the score is not treated as species identification. Equal-diffusion ablation drops the amplitude ratio to 0.0078. The radial PDE peak k = 3.115 versus infinite-line k_c = 3.272 (ratio 0.952) is the bounded-disk shift. Overall 88.8/100 (faithfulness 88.2, reproducibility 90.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_simulans_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-simulans-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 519627 B, 1260×840 px, artifact_sha256 816d722ff5c9d5c2cc697711552b6ec75bf10c31b838f7f9d4967e8daa325a78 (sha256 816d722ff5c9d5c2cc697711552b6ec75bf10c31b838f7f9d4967e8daa325a78), spec_fingerprint 60c689b8831f2a33a5b5821273a9d442392ad8ba957aa7d326024097a96f04cd. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 60c689b8831f2a33a5b5821273a9d442392ad8ba957aa7d326024097a96f04cd; artifact_sha256: 816d722ff5c9d5c2cc697711552b6ec75bf10c31b838f7f9d4967e8daa325a78; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_simulans_turing_wavelength_s0/Drosophila_simulans_female_wikimedia.jpg=8cf84002b7360579..., datasets/drosophila_simulans_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_simulans_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=cbf21999cb034540..., datasets/drosophila_simulans_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_simulans_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=d581f0b19b1f33bb..., datasets/drosophila_simulans_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=f6fa93b93eea80e6..., datasets/drosophila_simulans_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=b0435b2ab49a47d2...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-simulans-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite critical wavenumber from a reaction-diffusion instability. | Glassford 2015: the epandrial posterior lobe is a melanogaster-subgroup novelty. | Hagen 2020: simulans-clade lobes diverged within about the last 240,000 years. | Edwards 2007 documents Hawaiian picture-wing melanin; Huey 2000 documents the subobscura size cline.; reconstructed_in_script: λ_c = 1.92 µm is the slot assignment. Neighbour wavelengths 2.64 µm and 1.60 µm are γ retunings. | On a 96 µm arc the mode counts are 36 (silvestris), 50 (simulans), 60 (subobscura). | The plate annulus measures 67.57 µm (111 px scale bar = 100 µm), or 35.2 detail wavelengths per ring.; transfer_boundary: Silvestris and subobscura are catalog neighbours at 0 Ma, not phylogenetic ancestors. | The 1.92 µm law is not the 83 µm tergite-band model of slot 2701.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a published measurement of 1.92 µm granule spacing. | Does not claim the gallery plate is an electron micrograph of the clasper. | Does not claim GIF-to-plate CV similarity uniquely identifies D. simulans; the whole-fly control also scores 85.6.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Resolved in pass 2: odd-radius holdout Pearson r = 0.9895 is a measured row and a self-test gate.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Resolved in pass 2: plate CV similarity 89.5 and Wikimedia whole-fly CV 85.6 are both reported in the loop fitness JSON.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Resolved in pass 2: bounded_disk_k_ratio records numerical k / analytical k_c = 0.952. The gap is kept.', 'status': 'resolved'}",
            "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Still open: no independent second assessor in this session.', 'status': 'open'}" ;
        pk:hasScore "0.888"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor, pass 2; R4 second assessor still open)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

